#!/bin/sh
snapshot="$("$HOME/.local/bin/antonina-scheduler-snapshot" 2>/dev/null || printf '{}')"
exec timeout -k 15s 900s "$HOME/.local/bin/opencode-openclaw" run --auto --model opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free --variant low --dir /workspace/antonina "ANTONINA-SCHEDULER-TURN. Optimize wall-clock time by topology. Use CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.
FIRST ACTION: breadth. While unrepresented_projects is nonempty, inspect ONLY CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.unrepresented_issues; skip represented-project issue reads. CANDIDATE BUDGET: one compact issue read and at most one worktree lookup; never reread a skipped candidate.
Run antonina-scheduler-issue --issue ISSUE. Explicit complete/human/dependency blocker => skip immediately WITHOUT a worktree lookup. Else run antonina-scheduler-worktrees --issue ISSUE. [] => next. A returned cwd is registered, existing, and unoccupied: LAUNCH before another candidate. Unclear scope => bounded reconnaissance.
PRE-LAUNCH GATE: before second-agent/depth launch rerun antonina-scheduler-snapshot. If any project is newly unrepresented, continue from project breadth.
For a launch, first run collision-resistant base-16 ID generator: python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(6))'; use its output as AGENT_ID. Never guess/probe short IDs.
antonina board comment --id ISSUE --body BODY --author openclaw@marceline-dev --json
antonina agent new --id AGENT_ID --cwd CWD --title TITLE --json
antonina agent run --id AGENT_ID --cwd CWD --prompt PROMPT --detach --json
Never reuse a live cwd. Never use ls/find/globs over /workspace to discover cwd.
LIVE OWNERSHIP: CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.live_agents is authoritative. Never scan historical/finished agent inventories to reconstruct ownership. If a serialized queue has no live owner, launch one bounded reconciliation owner on an existing unoccupied registered cwd rather than reconstructing old holders yourself.
BREADTH BARRIER: no project gets a second live agent until every project_hint is represented or has a precise dependency/topology/collision blocker. AFTER BREADTH: do not idle. Inspect CURRENT_SNAPSHOT.represented_issue_candidates and test distinct open issues in represented projects for positive-speedup launches before considering complementary intra-issue fronts. After breadth, AssemblyP1 should have at least five useful agents whenever five independent positive-speedup fronts exist. Choose only actions with positive expected marginal wall-clock speedup after dependencies, overlap, collision risk, and reconciliation cost. AFTER EACH ACTION: rerun antonina-scheduler-snapshot, treat it as CURRENT_SNAPSHOT, and continue from project breadth. IDLE WATCH is allowed only after both sweeps found no positive-speedup launch: (1) every unrepresented project is represented or precisely blocked, and (2) represented_issue_candidates produced no launchable distinct issue or complementary front. Then sleep 20, refresh topology, and retry until watchdog/fatal error.
CURRENT_SNAPSHOT:
$snapshot"
